@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* No chrome at all: the body and nothing else.
   For pages whose surroundings must not depend on the address in the bar. MainLayout decides on the sidebar by asking
   AppShell.IsStandalonePage about the current path, which is the right rule for every ordinary page and the wrong one for a page
   that answers for an address the platform does not recognise: on a not-found render the path IS the mistyped address, so a
   path-based rule would draw the full application shell around it - offering a menu to a visitor who may not be signed in, and
   picking whose chrome to show for an address that belongs to no area. Declaring the layout on the page removes the question. *@
@Body
